# Copy to .sync.env to enable the schedule auto-sync (scripts/sync_schedule.sh).
#
# PREFERRED — ROS_CSV_URL: the "Publish to web" CSV of ONLY the
# "ROS Chart (auto)" tab. This keeps the master sheet's PII tabs private while
# giving the credential-free cron an anonymous fetch. To create it, the sheet
# owner (Elliot) does:
#   File → Share → Publish to web → (dropdown) "ROS Chart (auto)" → CSV → Publish
# then copies the generated URL, which looks like:
#   https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/e/2PACX-…/pub?gid=…&single=true&output=csv
ROS_CSV_URL=

# FALLBACK — SHEET_ID: the Google Sheet ID (docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/<ID>/edit).
# Only used if ROS_CSV_URL is empty. Requires the WHOLE file to be
# "Anyone with the link → Viewer", which exposes PII tabs — avoid for the
# master sheet.
SHEET_ID=

# No config needed for alerting: successful syncs post nothing, and failures
# (can't fetch / can't parse / deploy failed) auto-alert #pat-health as the Pat
# bot, throttled to once per 6h per issue. Pat must be a member of #pat-health.

# --- Attendee FAQ auto-sync (scripts/sync_faq.sh) --------------------------
# The FAQ hub page is published to web, but the DATABASE behind it is not
# publicly readable (embedded blocks return role "none" to anonymous calls), so
# unlike the schedule this needs a real Notion integration:
#   1. Create an internal integration: https://www.notion.so/my-integrations
#      → copy its secret (starts ntn_… or secret_…).
#   2. Open the FAQ database in Notion → ••• → Connections → add the integration.
#   3. Grab the database id (the 32-hex in its URL).
# Until both are set, sync_faq.sh skips cleanly.
NOTION_TOKEN=
FAQ_DATABASE_ID=
